================================================================================
Third-party software and attribution
================================================================================

Aquarium is built on top of, and depends on, software from the Sui project by
Mysten Labs, Inc. (https://github.com/MystenLabs/sui), which is licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0.

In particular, Aquarium links against the following Mysten Labs crates and does
NOT vendor or copy their source:

  - sui-data-store   (multi-tier object/transaction/epoch data store + GraphQL backend)
  - sui-types        (core Sui object, transaction and effects types)
  - sui-execution    (the Move VM / adapter execution engine)

It also links transitively against further Mysten Labs and Move crates (for
example move-core-types) pulled in by the crates above.

The design of Aquarium's execution glue (the adapter that exposes a
`sui_data_store::ObjectStore` to the Sui `Executor` via the runtime storage
traits, and the way input objects are resolved before execution) is derived
from, and follows the structure of, Mysten Labs' `sui-replay-2` crate
(crates/sui-replay-2 in the Sui repository). Where Aquarium's source follows
that structure closely, the relevant files carry an explicit attribution header.

All Mysten Labs source remains the copyright of Mysten Labs, Inc. and is used
under the terms of the Apache License, Version 2.0.
